# Logs
#
# Anchored. A bare `logs` matches a directory of that name at *any* depth, and
# it silently swallowed web/src/logs/ — four React components the dashboard
# imports — so a clean checkout could not typecheck or build the web app, and
# therefore could not produce the release binary that embeds it. The files were
# present on every machine that had ever built it, which is why nobody noticed.
/logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
